      "text_raw": "The same principle can be\napplied to more than two\ndifferential pairs. Four of\nthem are placed in parallel\nin order to increase the input\nrange. In this example, an\ninput range is obtained of\napproximately 160 mV ,\nptp\nwhich is about ten times\nlarger than for a single\ndifferential pair for the same\ndistortion (0.8% variation in\ntransconductance).\nThe transconductance is\nreduced to about 35% of the\ndifferential pair with the\nsame total current.",
